 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "$ABCD$ is a parallelogram where $A({=a1}, {=a2})$, $B({=b1}, {=b2})$ and $C({=c1}, {=c2})$. Find the coordinates of the point $D$. Write your answer as $(x, y)$.",
 "solution": [
  "The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other, so the intersection point $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{AC}$.",
  "$M\\left(\\frac{({=a1})+({=c1})}{2}, \\frac{({=a2})+({=c2})}{2}\\right)=M({=m1}, {=m2})$.",
  "$M$ is also the midpoint of $\\overline{BD}$. Let $D(x_1, y_1)$.",
  "${=m1}=\\frac{({=b1})+x_1}{2}$, so $({=b1})+x_1={=2*m1}$, hence $x_1={=d1}$.",
  "${=m2}=\\frac{({=b2})+y_1}{2}$, so $({=b2})+y_1={=2*m2}$, hence $y_1={=d2}$.",
  "Therefore $D({=d1}, {=d2})$."
 ],
